  @@ -9,5 +9,5 @@ stated precisely. Captures live under `docs/evidence/v1.1.4/tui/<defect>/`.
  -| D-06 | major | FIXED | `e4d9b1fd` | `cli/test/provider_status_plain.test.ts` "D-06" (7 cases: one key across attempts and a counter, what/bound/cancel, five failure classes in plain words, raw cause in `detail` with credentials redacted, clamped countdown, probe silence and plain final failure, optional protocol fields); Rust `live_state::tests::identical_provider_waits_collapse_into_one_row_with_a_counter`, `a_new_turn_gets_its_own_status_row_and_other_notices_do_not_merge`, `details_shows_the_raw_cause_while_the_turn_waits`, `details_without_a_provider_error_says_so`; `live_view::tests::a_long_wait_shows_one_status_row_with_the_counter_at_every_width` (40/60/100 cols), `the_wait_has_one_timer_not_two`; `protocol::tests::a_notice_carries_an_optional_key_and_raw_cause_and_an_old_one_still_parses` | A provider wait is one transcript row per turn that updates in place: cause in plain words (credentials, quota, rate limit, overloaded, restarting, timeout, unreachable), `Retry N`, next attempt in Ns, how long until Nexus gives up (the controller's existing deadline), `esc cancels`. The raw cause (condition, HTTP status, provider message, request id) is kept out of the text and shown by `/details`, redacted. The status line keeps one timer. `notice` gained optional `key` and `detail`; an older TUI shows each as a plain line, an older sidecar's notices render as before. Limitations: the retry bound is the time deadline (20 min, 2 min before first contact), not an attempt count; the turn banner after a final failure still shows the provider's own error text (`inferenceFailure.message`); `/details` is handled by the TUI and is not in the sidecar's command catalogue, so it is not offered by completion (the status row names it). Captures: `docs/evidence/v1.1.4/tui/D-06/` |
  -| D-07 | major | FIXED | `e4d9b1fd` | `cli/test/provider_status_plain.test.ts` "D-07" (4 cases: guidance text with next steps and no raw cause, rejected-credentials wording, a dead endpoint refuses the prompt with `NO_PROVIDER` and starts no turn and no retry loop, a recovered provider accepts the prompt); Rust `live_state::tests::a_prompt_refused_for_want_of_a_provider_goes_back_to_the_composer_with_the_reason`, `a_refused_prompt_does_not_overwrite_what_was_typed_meanwhile`; `live_view::tests::a_first_run_without_a_provider_shows_the_next_step_at_every_width` (40/60/100 cols) | With no usable provider the start-up notice says what is missing (`No model is connected: nothing answers at <endpoint>` or credentials rejected), `/connect`, a local model server (LM Studio, Ollama, llama.cpp), `nexus doctor` and `docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`; the cause chain is in `/details`. A prompt sent while start-up found no provider is probed again (3 s, so a server started or `/connect` done since is honoured) and, if still down, refused with the reason (the TUI puts the draft back in the composer when it is empty) instead of entering the retry loop. New: error code `NO_PROVIDER` (older TUIs show `NO_PROVIDER: <message>` and the draft is not restored). Limitations: the TUI does not open the connect panel by itself (the notice names it); steering and follow-up turns started from a refused state are not gated; the header still shows the configured model name (the placeholder `local-model` when none); a provider that goes down after start-up is handled by the D-06 wait, not this refusal. Captures: `docs/evidence/v1.1.4/tui/D-07/` |
  +| D-06 | major | FIXED | `e4d9b1fd`, `92a68252`, round-2 commit (this push) | `cli/test/provider_status_plain.test.ts` "D-06" (8 cases: one key across attempts and a counter, what/bound/cancel, five failure classes in plain words, raw cause in `detail` with credentials redacted, clamped countdown, probe silence and plain final failure, optional protocol fields, and recovery keeps the earlier error in detail, labelled); Rust `live_state::tests::identical_provider_waits_collapse_into_one_row_with_a_counter`, `a_new_turn_gets_its_own_status_row_and_other_notices_do_not_merge`, `details_shows_the_raw_cause_while_the_turn_waits`, `details_without_a_provider_error_says_so`; `live_view::tests::a_long_wait_shows_one_status_row_with_the_counter_at_every_width` (40/60/100 cols), `the_wait_has_one_timer_not_two`; `protocol::tests::a_notice_carries_an_optional_key_and_raw_cause_and_an_old_one_still_parses` | A provider wait is one transcript row per turn that updates in place: cause in plain words (credentials, quota, rate limit, overloaded, restarting, timeout, unreachable), `Retry N`, next attempt in Ns, how long until Nexus gives up (the controller's existing deadline), `esc cancels`. The raw cause (condition, HTTP status, provider message, request id) is kept out of the text and shown by `/details`, redacted and with every URL cut to scheme, host and path (no userinfo, query or fragment; tested with placeholder credentials). The status line keeps one timer. `notice` gained optional `key` and `detail`; an older TUI shows each as a plain line, an older sidecar's notices render as before. Limitations: the retry bound is the time deadline (20 min, 2 min before first contact), not an attempt count; the turn banner after a final failure still shows the provider's own error text (`inferenceFailure.message`); `/details` is handled by the TUI and is not in the sidecar's command catalogue, so it is not offered by completion (the status row names it). Captures: `docs/evidence/v1.1.4/tui/D-06/` |
  +| D-07 | major | FIXED | `e4d9b1fd`, `92a68252`, round-2 commit (this push) | `cli/test/provider_status_plain.test.ts` describes "D-07: first run without a provider" (4), "D-07 review round 2" (6: /models 401 and 403 with working chat run the prompt, a steer and a deferred follow-up on a dead provider are refused instead of run, a refused prompt is not in history, no URL credential in any rendered string) and "D-07 review follow-ups" (1: a prompt sent before the start-up probe ends is gated); Rust `live_state::tests::a_prompt_refused_for_want_of_a_provider_goes_back_to_the_composer_with_the_reason`, `a_refused_prompt_does_not_overwrite_what_was_typed_meanwhile`, `a_refused_prompt_with_a_paste_comes_back_as_the_paste_label_not_its_expansion`; `live_view::tests::a_first_run_without_a_provider_shows_the_next_step_at_every_width` (40/60/100 cols) | When start-up finds nothing answering (connection refused, DNS, timeout) the notice says what is missing (`No model is connected: nothing answers at <endpoint>`), `/connect`, a local model server (LM Studio, Ollama, llama.cpp), `nexus doctor` and `docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`; the cause chain is in `/details`. Only that state gates: a prompt, a steer that would start a turn and a deferred follow-up all go through one `gatedTurn` that waits for the start-up probe, probes again (3 s, so a server started or `/connect` done since is honoured) and, if still down, refuses with the reason (`NO_PROVIDER` for a prompt; the steer acknowledgement `cancelled` with the text returned for steer and follow-up) instead of entering the retry loop; a refused message is not added to prompt history, and the TUI restores the whole draft, paste buffers included, when its composer is empty. A 401 or 403 on the start-up `/models` probe is only a warning (`rejected the credentials on the start-up check; Nexus will still try your messages`): it never blocks, because the chat path refreshes tokens and may accept a key the model list refuses. New: error code `NO_PROVIDER` (older TUIs show `NO_PROVIDER: <message>` and do not restore the draft). Limitations: the TUI does not open the connect panel by itself (the notice names it); a cancelled re-probe leaves the gate in place without a dedicated test; the header still shows the configured model name (the placeholder `local-model` when none); a provider that goes down after start-up is handled by the D-06 wait, not this refusal. Captures: `docs/evidence/v1.1.4/tui/D-07/` |
  +2 -2

